(\"huntress_feature.bin\")` via `splitSourceDirs` + `ZipFile`, 16 B folded as\n2 big-endian u64. 9 old-day sets solved by the solver (d11/d13/d21 first time v2, pure chains). Prebuild\n`v2-split-asset-read` closed the gap overnight.\n\n**Day 27 — Dependency Surface** (`CONTROL=\"legacy_dependency\"`, `STRUCTURAL=\"reachable challenge-owned dependency\"`;\nprompt \"Prove which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface\"; MainActivity: \"cross the\nreachable challenge-owned dependency boundary\"). 0 wrong, all first try, NO LLM work: single CORRECT ~6 s from start\n(solver race; the worker only printed READY), TT 3.0 s (solve 0.17 s), 11-set Mastery 3.4 s (solve 0.40 s).\n- Artifact: the plain 12.7 KB 6-entry fixture in single AND TT (`dependency_surface{,_time_trial}.apk`); manifest\n  deep link `huntress27://dependency-surface/unlock` on the exported `.ChallengeActivity`; no library code, no extra dex.\n- Puzzle v1 `{\"codec\":\"base64\",\"data\":\"QU5TLT...\"}` in single and TT -> `base64 -d` = the answer. **v2 is GONE today in\n  every mode**: TT is the d17-d22 shape again (dex 2680 B: tag dropped, `STRUCTURAL` + stub `DependencySurface\n  .exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1`, never called). The \"dependency flaw\" exists only as words.\n- Mastery 11 sets, ALL v1, each with its source day's original codec + rolled key (list under Variant axes); set10 =\n  d26 `.apks` with the v1 base+feature fragment; set8 = d20 `dynamic` -> `assets/payload.dex`. Carried-over solver\n  (`extract_answer` / codec decoders / `_split_bundle`) covered all 11.\n- GM spelling unchanged (`answer` / `setN.answer`, `exact`, `ANS-` + 16 uppercase hex).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- One field, `answer`. Single solve and TT use id `answer`; Mastery uses `setN.answer` (3, 5-11 sets; 11 on d27).\n- Format `ANS-` + exactly 16 UPPERCASE hex, normalization `exact`. v2 code already emits uppercase via the hex table.\n- No worker-derived mobile