resolution True 1\nmobile-android:native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks True 2\nmobile-android:native-gated-branch-read True 1\nmobile-android:native-init-array-decrypt True 1\nmobile-android:native-inline-syscall-stubs True 1\nmobile-android:native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate True 1\nmobile-android:native-payload-system-load True 1\nmobile-android:native-so-emulate-export True 1\nmobile-android:native-stack-string True 1\nmobile-android:native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs True 1\nmobile-android:nested-container-recurse True 1\nmobile-android:opaque-predicate-dead-branch True 1\nmobile-android:payload-digest-pinned-select True 1\nmobile-android:payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap True 1\nmobile-android:permutation-transposition-family True 1\nmobile-android:pinned-emulator-env-profile False 2\nmobile-android:play-integrity-verdict-select True 2\nmobile-android:probe-arg-resolve-before-stub True 1\nmobile-android:process-exec-shell-probe-stubs True 1\nmobile-android:proguard-mapping-restore True 1\nmobile-android:proof-flow-candidate-ranking True 1\nmobile-android:protobuf-asset-wire-decode True 1\nmobile-android:proxy-methodhandle-invokecustom True 1\nmobile-android:puzzle-entry-pointer-follow True 2\nmobile-android:puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields True 1\nmobile-android:r8-renamed-chain-follow True 1\nmobile-android:reflection-name-resolve True 1\nmobile-android:registernatives-table True 1\nmobile-android:resource-id-const-resolve True 1\nmobile-android:rolling-xor-keystream-family True 1\nmobile-android:root-signal-vector-key True 1\nmobile-android:sdk-int-platform-gate False 1\nmobile-android:split-config-device-select True 1\nmobile-android:split-feature-dex-code True 1\nmobile-android:split-native-lib-config-abi True 1\nmobile-android:split-resources-arsc-overlay True 1\nmobile-android:split-signature-digest-binding True 1\nmobile-android:sqlcipher-asset-decrypt True 1\nmobile-android:static-key-cipher-decode True 1\nmobile-android:timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs True 1\nmobile-android:tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret True 1\nmobile-android:utf16-string-pool-scan True 1\nmobile-android:v1-manifest-digest-verify True 1\nmobile-android:v2-app-state-first-run-defaults True 1\nmobile-android:v2-boolean-gate-manifest-facts True 1\nmobile-android:v2-debugger-gate-state-loop True 1\nmobile-android:v2-dexloader-payload-invoke True 1\nmobile-android:v2-reflection-api-breadth True 2\nmobile-android:v2-split-asset-read True 1\nmobile-android:v2-string-decrypt-name-resolve True 1\nmobile-android:webview-asset-js-scan True 1\nmobile-android:whitebox-table-cipher-eval True 1\nmobile-android:xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack True 1\nmobile-android:zip-slip-entry-normalize True 1\nmobile-android:zip-structure-anomaly-scan True 1\n1:# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D27 seen, D28+ forecast)\n94:## Concept table\n213:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n272:## Readiness gaps\n324:  {\"id\": \"dependency-sbom-inventory\", \"concept\": \"bundled third-party dependency inventory (rows 106-108): library packages outside the app package, versions and their source\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 theme `legacy_dependency` / STRUCTURAL 'reachable challenge-owned dependency' shipped as words only; a regeneration will likely bundle 2+ generated libs. Pure-python `lib.android.dependency_inventory(apk) -> [{pkg, name, version, source, classes, dex}]`: group dex classes by package prefix not under the manifest package (and not android/androidx/kotlin/java), read version from `META-INF/*.version` (androidx style 'x.y.z'), `META-INF/maven/<g>/<a>/pom.properties` (version=), `META-INF/*.kotlin_module`, static final String fields named VERSION/VERSION_NAME/LIB_VERSION in the lib's BuildConfig, `assets/*.jar|*.aar` members (recurse), `lib/<abi>/*.so` version strings (`OpenSSL 1.0.1`, `SQLite 3.x`). Expose as a candidate feature for solve.py: values tied to a lib (ANS- consts, flaw ids like `HCTF-DEP-*`) are tagged with the lib. Regression: synthetic APK with 3 lib packages + pom.properties; D27 fixtures must still return []. Pure python, <0.1 s/APK.\"},\n325:  {\"id\": \"exported-surface-sink-reachability\", \"concept\": \"several generated dependency flaws; only the one reachable from a manifest-EXPORTED component counts (rows 1, 8, 106)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 prompt: 'Prove which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface'; TT stub `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1`. Build on the existing entry-reachable-callgraph-rank, but start from EVERY exported component: parse the binary manifest for activity/activity-alias/service/receiver/provider with exported=true, or an intent-filter and no exported attr when targetSdk<31 (legacy implicit export), minus those guarded by a signature-level permission; entry methods onCreate/onNewIntent/onStartCommand/onBind/onReceive/query/insert/openFile/call/handleMessage. Walk invoke-static/virtual/direct/interface/super (+ reflection names already resolved by reflection-name-resolve, + Runnable/Handler/Thread.start edges) into lib packages; for each candidate value (ANS- const, flaw id, v2 Release-style chain) record reached/unreached; veto unreached ones in proof_flow ranking. Regression: synthetic APK with 3 libs x 1 flaw each, only one reached from an exported Activity, one from a non-exported Service (decoy), one dead.\"},\n326:  {\"id\": \"v2-boolean-gate-manifest-facts\", \"concept\": \"v2 gate with boolean/narrow args fed by manifest/PackageManager facts (`(ZI)I` exportedReachability; ActivityInfo.exported, permission, targetSdk)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If D27 returns as v2 (TT mutation or Mastery regeneration), the gate is `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1` -- first boolean-typed theme arg. Deep evaluator: correct Z/B/S/C arg + return semantics (if-eqz on Z, int-to-byte/short/char narrowing, boolean returned as int), and intrinsics returning REAL manifest facts: PackageManager.getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_ACTIVITIES|GET_SERVICES|GET_RECEIVERS|GET_PROVIDERS).activities[i].exported/name/permission, getActivityInfo(ComponentName, 0), resolveActivity/queryIntentActivities for the deep link `huntressNN://<slug>/unlock`, ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion/minSdkVersion/flags, ComponentInfo.exported default per targetSdk. Regression: synthetic chain where the boolean comes from ChallengeActivity's exported flag (true) and a decoy non-exported component (false -> -1).\"},\n327:  {\"id\": \"multidex-class-resolution\", \"concept\": \"multidex APK: classes2.dex..classesN.dex, chain spans dexes, duplicate class defs (first dex wins) (row 107)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every APK so far had one classes.dex; a real dependency surface ships libraries in a secondary dex. Ensure lib.android (puzzle_candidates, deep evaluator, strings scans, proof_flow, callgraph) loads classes.dex, classes2.dex, ... in numeric order (classes10 after classes9, not lexicographic), resolves a class to its FIRST definition (ART/PathClassLoader order), and lets the chain call across dexes (string/type/method ids are per-dex: never share index tables). Also: duplicate class in classes2 with a different ANS- const = decoy. Regression: split a fixture's chain classes across 2 dexes + a shadow copy in classes3.dex.\"},\n328:  {\"id\": \"schema-deescalation-guard\", \"concept\": \"timed schema can go BACK (D27: v2 vanished from TT and all 11 Mastery sets)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D27 was solved 3/3 only because v1 decoders still race first in solve.py. Keep that order: v1 puzzle `data` decode -> split-bundle fill -> v2 evaluator -> code scans; never skip v1 because the day number is >= 23 or because yesterday was v2; regression cases from every schema stay in solver/cases.\"},\n329:  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26: the cue for `*.apks` (list every member; the evidence lives in the OTHER split) is now in steps 0/1/5b. Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n330:  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D26 shipped a bare .apks (no toc.pb); config-split / AAB variants are now plausible. github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n331:  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n332:  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n333:  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-jar-dependency\", \"concept\": \"dependency shipped as JVM bytecode (assets/*.jar, .aar -> classes.jar, *.class), not dex (row 108)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure-python class-file reader: magic CAFEBABE, constant pool (Utf8/Integer/Float/Long/Double/Class/String/Fieldref/Methodref/NameAndType/MethodHandle/InvokeDynamic; Long/Double take 2 slots), fields with ConstantValue attribute (static finals), methods' Code attribute; tiny JVM interpreter for static pure methods (iconst/ldc/ldc2_w/lload/lstore/ladd/lsub/lmul/lxor/lor/land/lshl/lshr/lushr/l2i/i2l/invokestatic/ireturn/lreturn/if*/goto/tableswitch) so a v2-style chain into the jar evaluates. Walk nested zips (aar -> classes.jar -> *.class). Regression: synthetic jar with an ANS- const and a 2-method long chain; `javap -c -constants` (installed) for cross-checking while building only.\"},\n334:  {\"id\": \"dependency-version-advisory-match\", \"concept\": \"challenge-owned advisory list matched against bundled lib versions (semver, Maven ordering, lexicographic trap) (row 109)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'generated dependency flaw' suggests a generated advisory table (asset JSON or dex string array: id, package, affected range '<1.2.10', '[1.0,1.3)', fixed version) plus several lib versions. Implement version compare: numeric segments (1.2.10 > 1.2.9), Maven qualifiers (alpha<beta<milestone<rc<snapshot<''<sp), '-SNAPSHOT', 'v' prefix, build metadata '+x' ignored; range syntaxes npm/semver (^ ~ < <= >= ||), Maven interval [a,b), python-style '>=1.0,<2.0'. Return affected (lib, advisory) pairs; combine with exported-surface-sink-reachability to choose the one that is affected AND reachable. Regression: table where a lexicographic compare picks the wrong lib.\"},\n335:  {\"id\": \"deeplink-input-validation-eval\", \"concept\": \"exported deep-link handler validates its input (host/path allowlist, startsWith/endsWith/contains, regex, intent:// parseUri) -- the accepted argument feeds the answer (row 112)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"MASVS-CODE-4 is the natural follow-up to D27's 'exported mobile surface'. Model android.net.Uri semantics in the evaluator: Uri.parse never throws; getHost lowercases? (no: returns as given), getPath percent-decoded, getEncodedPath raw, getQueryParameter decodes %XX and '+' -> ' ' only via UrlQuerySanitizer (Uri keeps '+'), returns FIRST duplicate, getQueryParameters all; getLastPathSegment; Intent.parseUri('intent://...#Intent;scheme=..;S.key=val;end'). For validators with a finite accepted set (string equals, startsWith on a const, regex fullmatch with a literal), derive the accepted value and continue the chain with it; record the manifest deep link `huntressNN://<slug>/unlock` as the default input. Regression: synthetic handler where `host.endsWith(\\\"huntress.local\\\")` is bypassable and the chain mixes the accepted host.\"},\n336:  {\"id\": \"zip-slip-entry-normalize\", \"concept\": \"archive extraction in a dependency: entries with ../, absolute, backslash or duplicate names; only the entry that resolves to the checked path counts (row 110)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Classic vulnerable-dependency flaw (zip slip, CVE-2018 class). When an APK asset is a zip/jar that the dex extracts (ZipInputStream.getNextEntry + new File(dir, name) + FileOutputStream, or a lib unzip helper), resolve each entry like Java: File(dir,name) concatenation, getCanonicalPath() normalisation of '..' and '.', backslash kept as a literal char on Android, absolute names re-rooted under dir by File(parent, child), later duplicate entries overwrite earlier ones; then answer the dex's read of the target path (e.g. files/config.json or the code-cache dex). Use raw central-directory names (zipfile sanitises) -- read via the existing zip-structure-anomaly-scan parser. Regression: synthetic asset zip with 3 entries resolving to the same path.\"},\n337:  {\"id\": \"sdk-int-platform-gate\", \"concept\": \"branches on Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion (legacy platform behaviour, implicit export pre-31) (row 111)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'legacy_dependency' hints at legacy-platform behaviour too (MASVS-CODE-1). Evaluator intrinsics: Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / RELEASE / CODENAME from the pinned-emulator profile (keep the value in ONE place with pinned-emulator-env-profile; default API 34, RELEASE '14'), ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion from the APK's own <uses-sdk> (binary manifest), Build.VERSION_CODES constants inlined by javac (sget vs const). Exported default: android:exported absent + intent-filter -> exported iff targetSdk < 31. Regression: a chain that takes a different branch at targetSdk 30 vs 31.\"},\n338:  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26 repeat: the mastery generalize worker wrote a split-aware eval that never persisted in solve.py. D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json.\"},\n339:  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n340:  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n341:  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n342:  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n343:  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n344:  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"},\n345:  {\"id\": \"app-update-version-gate\", \"concept\": \"forced-update / minimum-version gate: PackageInfo.versionCode/versionName compared with an asset or dex minimum (MASVS-CODE-2) (row 109)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Supply PackageManager.getPackageInfo(own pkg).versionCode/longVersionCode/versionName from the binary manifest (the fixture has versionCode/versionName attrs), parse the asset's update policy (JSON minVersion/minCode/blocked list), and evaluate the comparison with the same version semantics as dependency-version-advisory-match (reuse it). The answer is the value on the branch the APK's real version takes. Regression: versionName '6.0.1' vs min '6.0.10' (lexicographic trap).\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d21e4ad2-2ce4-4150-a62f-2e8aa1a9e184","uuid":"1f86d786-7e6d-4bd8-b9a5-9195700c93cd","tim