{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgUh8iLxo7bxgtQdyNW7o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YM6VKnM2JUVujr83GPwBhF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndef done(i):\n    v=st.get('mobile-android:'+i)\n    return bool(v) and (v.get('ok') is True or (v.get('attempts') or 0)>=2)\na=s.index(\"```json\",s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")); b=s.index(\"```\",a+7)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a+7:b])\nbuilt=[g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild' and done(g['id'])]\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if not (g['action']=='prebuild' and done(g['id']))]\nprint(\"moved to built:\",built)\nfor g in gaps:\n    if g['id']=='schema-deescalation-guard':\n        g['concept']=\"timed schema flips both ways (D27 v2 vanished everywhere; D28 v2 back in TT + 12/12 sets)\"\n        g['detail']=\"D27 and D28 were both 3/3 only because solve.py races v1 decoders first AND keeps the v2 evaluator armed. Keep that order: v1 puzzle `data` decode -> split-bundle fill -> v2 evaluator -> code scans; never skip either path because of the day number or yesterday's schema; regression cases from every schema stay in solver/cases.\"\n    if g['id'] in ('deeplink-input-validation-eval','sdk-int-platform-gate'):\n        g['priority']=3\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"packet-frame-codec-family\",\"concept\":\"v1 `packet` codec and its mutations: framed hex with magic, length field, checksum (row 113)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 single: `data` = hex of `48 41 | len u8 | payload | xor8(all prior bytes)`; the solver only got it by hex-decode + `ANS-` SEARCH (no parser). Pure-python `lib.android.parse_frames(blob) -> [{magic, hdr, seq, nonce, payload, checksum_ok, offset}]`: accept hex/base64/raw input; learn the magic from the first 1-4 bytes (repeat occurrences => multi-frame); length field u8, u16 BE/LE, u32 BE, LEB128 varint, and length that counts payload only vs payload+checksum vs whole frame (choose the reading that tiles the blob exactly); checksum xor8/sum8/two's-complement sum8/CRC-8/CRC-16-CCITT(FALSE, XMODEM)/CRC-16-MODBUS/CRC32/Adler32/Fletcher16 over payload-only or header+payload (reuse checksum-family-identify); escaped streams (SLIP C0/DB, HDLC 7E/7D^20, COBS). Wire it into puzzle_candidates for codec names packet/frame/wire/tlv/stream/protocol and as a fallback for any hex `data` whose first 2 bytes repeat. Fullmatch ANS on the PAYLOAD. Regression: D28 single case + synthetic u16-BE/CRC16 and SLIP-escaped variants.\"},\n {\"id\":\"multi-frame-seq-nonce-reorder\",\"concept\":\"several frames with seq/nonce fields: reorder, drop replayed duplicates, stale nonces and bad-checksum decoys (row 114)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D28 prompt 'preserve nonce and ordering semantics' with only one frame shipped -> the natural TT/Mastery/capstone mutation. On top of parse_frames: identify the seq field (byte/u16 that is a permutation of 0..n-1 or 1..n across frames) and the nonce field (distinct per legit frame, repeated in a replay); rules: sort by seq; on duplicate seq keep the FIRST frame with a valid checksum and a never-seen nonce (replays reuse the nonce; report both orders as ranked candidates when ambiguous); drop frames whose checksum fails or whose nonce is <= the last accepted when nonces are monotonic (replay window); join payloads; also try ack/fragment flags (MORE_FRAGMENTS bit). Return ranked candidates fullmatching ANS. Regression: 4 shuffled frames + 1 replay + 1 bad-crc decoy that alone would give a different ANS.\"},\n {\"id\":\"nonce-keyed-frame-payload\",\"concept\":\"frame payload encrypted/xored with a per-frame nonce or counter (CTR-style keystream, nonce||counter IV)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Next escalation of 'nonce semantics': payload_i = plain ^ f(nonce, i) where f is nonce byte repeated, (nonce+i)&255, LCG(nonce), or AES-CTR/ChaCha20 with a dex key and IV = nonce||counter (pycryptodome). Solve by `ANS-` known plaintext on the first frame: test the keystream families (single byte, nonce+i, nonce^i, rotating nonce bytes, LCG with the dex's constants) and confirm on the remaining bytes being uppercase hex; for AES/ChaCha read key/nonce consts from the dex (dex_strings / const-wide / byte arrays). Regression: 3 synthetic frames with nonce+i keystream and one AES-CTR frame.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-bytebuffer-stream-intrinsics\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain parsing/building frames with java.nio.ByteBuffer, DataInput/OutputStream, java.util.zip.CRC32/Adler32 (row 113)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If D28 regenerates with real protocol code (TT mutation, Mastery d28 set, capstone), the deep Dalvik evaluator must model: ByteBuffer.allocate/wrap/order(ByteOrder.BIG_ENDIAN|LITTLE_ENDIAN)/put/putShort/putInt/putLong/get*/getShort(int)/position/flip/remaining/array; ByteArrayOutputStream write/toByteArray/size; DataOutputStream writeByte/writeShort/writeInt/writeLong/writeUTF (modified UTF-8 with u16 length); DataInputStream readUnsignedByte/readUnsignedShort/readInt/readLong/readFully; java.util.zip.CRC32/Adler32 update(byte[],off,len)/getValue; Integer/Long/Short.reverseBytes, Integer.toUnsignedLong, Byte.toUnsignedInt, Arrays.copyOfRange, System.arraycopy. Regression: synthetic chain that frames 3 ints into a ByteBuffer (LE), CRC32s it and folds the CRC into the token.\"},\n {\"id\":\"checksum-family-identify\",\"concept\":\"identify an unknown frame checksum/CRC from examples (xor8, sum8, CRC-8/16/32 variants, Adler, Fletcher, Luhn)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Shared helper for packet-frame-codec-family and multi-frame reorder: given (covered_bytes, check_bytes) pairs, test xor8, sum8, -sum8, ~sum8, CRC-8 (poly 07, 31 Maxim), CRC-16 CCITT-FALSE/XMODEM/KERMIT/MODBUS/ARC, CRC-32 (zlib) and CRC-32C, Adler-32, Fletcher-16/32, over the coverage choices (payload only, header+payload, len+payload, magic excluded), in BE and LE; return the family that matches ALL legit frames so the odd frame out is flagged as the decoy. Pure python (crcmod-free tables), <5 ms per frame set.\"},\n {\"id\":\"hmac-frame-replay-window\",\"concept\":\"authenticated frames: HMAC/tag per frame + nonce/timestamp replay window; only frames that verify and are fresh count\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Real 'nonce semantics' as MASVS-NETWORK/AUTH: each frame carries tag = HMAC-SHA256(key, hdr||nonce||payload)[:N] with the key in dex consts (or derived from the package/build), plus a nonce/counter/timestamp; the receiver accepts a frame only if the tag verifies and the nonce was not seen (or counter > last, or |ts - now| <= window with now = a dex const). Implement verify with hashlib/hmac over candidate coverage layouts, then apply the window; return the payload of the accepted frames in order. Evaluator side: javax.crypto.Mac.getInstance/init(SecretKeySpec)/update/doFinal intrinsics. Regression: 3 good frames, 1 replay with valid tag, 1 forged tag.\"},\n {\"id\":\"request-signing-canonical-reconstruct\",\"concept\":\"reconstruct the app's backend request: canonical string (method, path, sorted query, body hash, nonce, timestamp) + HMAC signature header (row 115)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Reconstruct the app-to-backend protocol' may next ship real client code: Retrofit interface annotations (@GET/@POST path, @Query, @Header, @Field) in dex annotation sets, OkHttp Request.Builder/addHeader/HttpUrl.Builder, HttpURLConnection setRequestProperty. Pure python: read Retrofit annotation element values from the dex annotations_directory; evaluator intrinsics for StringBuilder/String.join/TreeMap sorted keys/URLEncoder.encode (application/x-www-form-urlencoded: space -> '+')/Uri.Builder/MessageDigest SHA-256 hex/Base64.encodeToString(NO_WRAP|URL_SAFE)/Mac. Output: the header value or code the app would send for the case ref/attempt in the contract. Regression: synthetic client signing 'POST\\\\n/mobile/attempt/<id>\\\\ncase_id=..&nonce=..\\\\n<sha256(body)>'.\"},\n {\"id\":\"rpc-stream-frame-decode\",\"concept\":\"gRPC / WebSocket / MQTT / length-prefixed protobuf streams in an asset or `data` (row 116)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Decoders: gRPC message = flag u8 (0/1 compressed gzip) + BE u32 length + protobuf (reuse protobuf-asset-wire-decode); WebSocket frame = FIN/opcode byte, mask bit + 7/16/64-bit length, 4-byte mask key xored over payload, continuation frames joined; MQTT fixed header + remaining-length varint, PUBLISH topic u16-prefixed + payload; Java DataOutputStream writeUTF records; netty LengthFieldBasedFrameDecoder-style u16/u32 prefixes. Expose via parse_frames' format probe; fullmatch ANS in any decoded string field. Regression: synthetic gRPC + masked WebSocket + MQTT blobs.\"},\n {\"id\":\"tlv-varint-record-parse\",\"concept\":\"TLV records (1-byte tag, u8/u16/varint length) and ASN.1-DER-like nesting inside a payload; answer = value of the named tag\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Protocol payloads often nest TLVs: parse T(1-2 B) L(u8 | u16 BE | BER long form 0x81/0x82 | LEB128) V recursively, recognise DER (SEQUENCE 0x30, OCTET STRING 0x04, UTF8String 0x0c, INTEGER 0x02); select the tag the dex reads (const compared against the tag byte) else every string value; zigzag decode for signed varints. Regression: synthetic payload with 3 TLVs where the ANS is split over tags 0x10 and 0x11 in tag order.\"},\n {\"id\":\"capstone-multi-mechanic-chain\",\"concept\":\"capstone APK combining several earlier mechanics in ONE chain (split read + JNI hop + reflection + decrypt loop + frame parse)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"3 days remain (D29-D31) and D31 is the likely all-days finale. Build a synthetic regression APK set whose v2 Release.code chain calls, in order: readSplit bytes from a feature split, a native nativeShare(long,int) export (unicorn), Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod dispatch, a byte[] decryptByte loop, a ByteBuffer-framed CRC, and a 7-round int[8] table walk; plus a v1 twin whose `data` nests codecs (packet -> base64 -> xor). Assert puzzle_candidates + solve.py fallback chain return the right ANS in <1 s, and that a 15-set Mastery of such APKs stays under the 6-7 s window (extend mastery-set-scaling-bench numbers). Fix whatever aborts (shared memo, per-APK time budget, abort reasons logged).\"},\n]\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g['action']!='prebuild' or g['priority']<=2 and False] + []  # placeholder\nEOF\necho"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1571,"cache_read_input_tokens":134337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1571},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d21e4ad2-2ce4-4150-a62f-2e8aa1a9e184","uuid":"bfd0408b-3726-4460-bcd7-e2eb2892c2c4","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:13:04.461Z","request_id":"req_011CgUh8hz8otB8h1CjZqqDD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YM6VKnM2JUVujr83GPwBhF":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndef done(i):\n    v=st.get('mobile-android:'+i)\n    return bool(v) and (v.get('ok') is True or (v.get('attempts') or 0)>=2)\na=s.index(\"```json\",s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\")); b=s.index(\"```\",a+7)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a+7:b])\nbuilt=[g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild' and done(g['id'])]\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if not (g['action']=='prebuild' an